---
layout: layouts/page.njk
styles: [section-nav, visa-info]
title: "Visa info"
description: "F-1-D Digital Nomad Visa eligibility, income thresholds, documents, and requirements."
---
<div class="visa-page" id="top">

  <div class="visa-hero">
    <div class="visa-hero__main">
      <span class="visa-hero__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h1>Digital Nomad visa</h1>
      <div class="visa-hero__ko">{{ visaRules.nameKo }}</div>
      <p class="visa-hero__intro">A visa designed for employees of overseas companies who can work remotely.</p>
      <p class="visa-hero__note">Introduced as a pilot in January 2024, the visa became permanent on {{ visaRules.effectiveFrom | formatDate }}. The permanent visa rules lowered the income threshold for applicants under {{ visaRules.ageBands[0].maxAge + 1 }} or those staying outside the capital region, and extended the maximum stay from two years to three.</p>
      <div class="visa-hero__updated">Last updated: {{ visaRules.lastUpdated | formatDate }}</div>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-facts">
      <div class="visa-facts__row">
        <div class="visa-facts__label">Status code</div>
        <div class="visa-facts__value visa-facts__value--tabular">{{ visaRules.statusCode }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-facts__row">
        <div class="visa-facts__label">Entry type</div>
        <div class="visa-facts__value">{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.entryType }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-facts__row">
        <div class="visa-facts__label">Period of stay</div>
        <div class="visa-facts__value visa-facts__value--tabular">
          <div class="visa-facts__value-main">{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.initialStayYears }} year, up to {{ visaRules.additionalFacts.maxStayYears }} years</div>
          <div class="visa-facts__value-note">+{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.extensionIncrementYears }} year per extension</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-facts__row">
        <div class="visa-facts__label">Who can join you</div>
        <div class="visa-facts__value">{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.accompanyingFamily }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-facts__row">
        <div class="visa-facts__label">Work inside Korea</div>
        <div class="visa-facts__value">{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.workInsideKoreaShort }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-facts__row">
        <div class="visa-facts__label">Change of status in&nbsp;Korea</div>
        <div class="visa-facts__value visa-facts__value--tabular">From {{ visaRules.additionalFacts.convertibleFromVisas | join(", ") }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-nav">
    <div class="section-nav__links">
      <a href="#who"><span class="section-nav__full">Eligibility</span><span class="section-nav__short">Eligibility</span></a>
      <a href="#documents"><span class="section-nav__full">Documents</span><span class="section-nav__short">Docs</span></a>
      <a href="#notes"><span class="section-nav__full">Important notes</span><span class="section-nav__short">Notes</span></a>
      <a href="#questions"><span class="section-nav__full">Questions</span><span class="section-nav__short">FAQ</span></a>
      <a href="#links"><span class="section-nav__full">Useful links</span><span class="section-nav__short">Links</span></a>
    </div>
    <a href="#top" class="section-nav__top" aria-label="Back to top"><span class="section-nav__top-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav__top-label">Top</span></a>
  </div>

  <section id="who" class="visa-section">
    <div class="visa-section__head">
      <span class="visa-section__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2>Eligibility</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="visa-body">The visa is available to applicants who meet all of the following requirements.</p>

    <div class="visa-checklist">
      <div class="visa-checklist__item">
        <svg class="visa-checklist__icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8.2l3.2 3.1L12.5 4" stroke="#0F7B54" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
        <div class="visa-checklist__text"><span class="visa-checklist__title">Age {{ visaRules.additionalFacts.minApplicantAge }} or over</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-checklist__item">
        <svg class="visa-checklist__icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8.2l3.2 3.1L12.5 4" stroke="#0F7B54" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
        <div class="visa-checklist__text"><span class="visa-checklist__title">Employed by a company outside Korea and able to work remotely</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-checklist__item">
        <svg class="visa-checklist__icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8.2l3.2 3.1L12.5 4" stroke="#0F7B54" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
        <div class="visa-checklist__text"><span class="visa-checklist__title">At least one year in the same industry</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-checklist__item">
        <svg class="visa-checklist__icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8.2l3.2 3.1L12.5 4" stroke="#0F7B54" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
        <div class="visa-checklist__text"><span class="visa-checklist__title">Private medical insurance</span><span class="visa-checklist__detail"> — at least {{ visaRules.additionalFacts.healthInsuranceMinCoverageKrw | krwShort }} of cover valid for the whole stay.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-checklist__item">
        <svg class="visa-checklist__icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8.2l3.2 3.1L12.5 4" stroke="#0F7B54" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
        <div class="visa-checklist__text"><span class="visa-checklist__title">Income requirement</span><span class="visa-checklist__detail"> — the threshold depends on your age and region of stay; see below.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="income" class="visa-subhead">
      <span class="visa-subhead__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h3>Income by age and region</h3>
    </div>
    <p class="visa-body">Income thresholds are set as a multiple of Korea’s per-capita GNI for the year before application. For {{ visaRules.gniReferenceYear }}, the GNI reference figure is ₩{{ visaRules.gniPerCapitaKrw | krw }}.</p>

    <div class="visa-income-note">Capital area means Seoul, Incheon and Gyeonggi-do, excluding population-decline areas.</div>

    <div class="visa-income-table-wrap">
      <table class="visa-income-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">Capital area<div class="visa-income-table__subhead">Seoul, Incheon, Gyeonggi-do — excluding population-decline areas</div></th>
            <th scope="col">Elsewhere<div class="visa-income-table__subhead">Other regions, plus Gyeonggi-do's population-decline areas</div></th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for band in visaRules.ageBands %}
          <tr>
            <td>{% if band.maxAge %}Age {{ band.minAge }}–{{ band.maxAge }}{% else %}Age {{ band.minAge }} and over{% endif %}</td>
            <td>{{ band.multiplierCapitalArea }} × GNI<div class="visa-income-table__mult">₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier[band.multiplierCapitalArea] | krw }}</div></td>
            <td>{{ band.multiplierNonCapitalArea }} × GNI<div class="visa-income-table__mult">₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier[band.multiplierNonCapitalArea] | krw }}</div></td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
          <tr class="visa-income-table__family">
            <td>Bringing family<div class="visa-income-table__submeta">Spouse or minor children</div></td>
            <td>{{ visaRules.familyMultiplier.multiplierCapitalArea }} × GNI<div class="visa-income-table__mult">₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier[visaRules.familyMultiplier.multiplierCapitalArea] | krw }}</div></td>
            <td>{{ visaRules.familyMultiplier.multiplierNonCapitalArea }} × GNI<div class="visa-income-table__mult">₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier[visaRules.familyMultiplier.multiplierNonCapitalArea] | krw }}</div></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-income-cards">
      {% for band in visaRules.ageBands %}
      <div class="visa-income-card">
        <div class="visa-income-card__head">{% if band.maxAge %}Age {{ band.minAge }}–{{ band.maxAge }}{% else %}Age {{ band.minAge }} and over{% endif %}</div>
        <div class="visa-income-card__row">
          <div class="visa-income-card__region">Capital area</div>
          <div class="visa-income-card__amount">{{ band.multiplierCapitalArea }} × GNI<div class="visa-income-table__mult">₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier[band.multiplierCapitalArea] | krw }}</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="visa-income-card__row">
          <div class="visa-income-card__region">Elsewhere</div>
          <div class="visa-income-card__amount">{{ band.multiplierNonCapitalArea }} × GNI<div class="visa-income-table__mult">₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier[band.multiplierNonCapitalArea] | krw }}</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
      <div class="visa-income-card">
        <div class="visa-income-card__head">Bringing family<div class="visa-income-card__head-note">Spouse or minor children</div></div>
        <div class="visa-income-card__row">
          <div class="visa-income-card__region">Capital area</div>
          <div class="visa-income-card__amount">{{ visaRules.familyMultiplier.multiplierCapitalArea }} × GNI<div class="visa-income-table__mult">₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier[visaRules.familyMultiplier.multiplierCapitalArea] | krw }}</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="visa-income-card__row">
          <div class="visa-income-card__region">Elsewhere</div>
          <div class="visa-income-card__amount">{{ visaRules.familyMultiplier.multiplierNonCapitalArea }} × GNI<div class="visa-income-table__mult">₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier[visaRules.familyMultiplier.multiplierNonCapitalArea] | krw }}</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-income-footnotes">
      <div>The multiplier is set by the visa rules; the GNI figure is updated annually by the Bank of Korea.</div>
      <div>The family multiplier applies regardless of your age.</div>
    </div>
    <a href="/#calculator" class="visa-inline-link">Eligibility calculator →</a>
  </section>

  <section id="documents" class="visa-section">
    <div class="visa-section__head">
      <span class="visa-section__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2>Documents</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="visa-body">An embassy or consulate may ask for additional documents or waive some requirements. Rules on document age, translation and legalization may also vary. Double-check with the office you apply through.</p>

    <div class="visa-doc-grid">
      <div class="visa-doc-card">
        <div class="visa-doc-card__title">General</div>
        <div class="visa-doc-card__list">
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Application form (Form 17)</span></div>
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Passport</span></div>
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>One standard-format photograph</span></div>
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Application fee</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-doc-card">
        <div class="visa-doc-card__title">For this visa</div>
        <div class="visa-doc-card__list">
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Proof of overseas employment or overseas business ownership</span></div>
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Proof of at least one year of relevant work experience</span></div>
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Income proof — payslips, bank statements or similar</span></div>
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Certificate of medical insurance</span></div>
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Criminal record certificate</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-doc-card">
        <div class="visa-doc-card__title">Only if it applies to you</div>
        <div class="visa-doc-card__list">
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Family relationship documents, if accompanied by family</span></div>
          <div class="visa-doc-card__item"><span class="visa-doc-card__dot">·</span><span>Proof of regional stay, when applying for a lower regional multiplier</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="notes" class="visa-section">
    <div class="visa-section__head">
      <span class="visa-section__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2>Important notes</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="visa-body">A few points require checking with relevant institutions.</p>

    <div class="visa-notes-grid">
      <div class="visa-note-card">
        <div class="visa-note-card__meta">
          <span class="visa-note-card__tag">Regional stay</span>
          <span class="visa-note-card__status">Ask the embassy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="visa-note-card__title">What proof of stay is enough?</div>
        <div class="visa-note-card__body">The visa rules list either a lease agreement or an accommodation reservation confirmation for at least one month.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-note-card">
        <div class="visa-note-card__meta">
          <span class="visa-note-card__tag">Insurance</span>
          <span class="visa-note-card__status">Ask NHIS</span>
        </div>
        <div class="visa-note-card__title">Both private and NHI are required?</div>
        <div class="visa-note-card__body">Six months of residence generally means <a href="{{ visaRules.nhisUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">joining National Health Insurance ↗</a>, while full-stay private insurance is required for application.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="visa-note-card">
        <div class="visa-note-card__meta">
          <span class="visa-note-card__tag">Tax</span>
          <span class="visa-note-card__status">Ask a tax adviser</span>
        </div>
        <div class="visa-note-card__title">Will I owe Korean tax?</div>
        <div class="visa-note-card__body">More than 183 days in Korea makes you a Korean tax resident. Foreign residents who have stayed in Korea less than 5 years over the past 10 years are subject to a <a href="{{ visaRules.foreignIncomeTaxRuleUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">special rule ↗</a> for foreign-source income. Ask a tax adviser or the <a href="{{ visaRules.natlTaxServiceUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">National Tax Service ↗</a>.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="questions" class="visa-section">
    <div class="visa-section__head">
      <span class="visa-section__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-faq">
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">Should I get a residence card?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">Yes. Anyone staying in Korea for more than 91 days must register as a resident and receive a residence card within 90 days of arrival. It is commonly called an ARC and is useful for opening a bank account, getting a phone contract and signing a long-term lease.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">Can I work for a Korean company?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">No. Employment and any profit-making activities in Korea are restricted on this visa. Employment by a Korean company requires a different status. Once in Korea, for questions about profit-making activities, consult {{ visaRules.immigrationContactCenterPhone }} on your individual case.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">Am I eligible as a freelancer?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">The published rule covers overseas business owners and people employed by overseas companies. It doesn’t address freelancers specifically. A freelancer with a registered overseas business might be eligible, check with the embassy handling your application.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">Does this time count toward permanent residence?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">The published F‑1‑D visa rules do not address this. Ask the Immigration Contact Center ({{ visaRules.immigrationContactCenterPhone }}) or the embassy handling your case.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">Can I switch from another visa while in Korea?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">Yes. If you meet the requirements, the published rules explicitly allow a change of status from B‑1, B‑2 or C‑3, and may allow changes from other statuses as well. Check your case with the Immigration Contact Center ({{ visaRules.immigrationContactCenterPhone }}) and use form 34 to apply.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">Can my family come with me?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">Yes. A spouse and minor children can accompany you. This raises the required GNI multiplier to 2 × in the capital area and 1.5 × elsewhere, regardless of your age.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">Do I need this visa to visit Korea?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">No. Depending on your nationality, you may be able to visit with K‑ETA or a short-term visa. The F‑1‑D visa allows eligible remote workers to stay longer, for up to three years. If you plan to work remotely while on a short-stay status, consult the Immigration Contact Center ({{ visaRules.immigrationContactCenterPhone }}).</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">Which nationalities can apply?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">There is no separate country list for the F‑1‑D, unlike the Working Holiday (H‑1) visa, which is based on agreements with participating countries.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">What insurance should I get?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">It should be private medical insurance covering at least {{ visaRules.additionalFacts.healthInsuranceMinCoverageKrw | krwShort }} for hospital treatment and repatriation to the home country during your full stay.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">How do I prepare a criminal record certificate?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">Generally, it should be legalized (apostilled or consular legalization), accompanied by a notarized translation, and issued within the previous 6 months. Rules may vary depending on your application embassy and the countries where you have lived.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">How do I calculate and convert my income?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">Use gross income (before tax) and convert it to KRW using the exchange rate on the day of application. This method was officially confirmed by the Ministry of Justice in October 2026 (inquiry <span class="visa-nowrap">1AA-2608-1171435</span>). You can double-check with the embassy handling your application.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="visa-faq__item">
        <summary class="visa-faq__summary"><span class="visa-faq__q">Can I reside in the Capital Area and still apply for the lower income threshold?</span><span class="visa-faq__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="visa-faq__a">Yes, in two cases: if you are aged 18–34 (1.5 × GNI) or reside in a <a href="/regions/gyeonggi-do/population-decline-areas/">population-decline area of <span class="visa-nowrap">Gyeonggi-do</span></a> (1–1.5 × GNI). The Ministry of Justice clarified this in October 2026 in response to inquiry <span class="visa-nowrap">1AA-2608-1171435</span>.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="links" class="visa-section">
    <div class="visa-section__head">
      <span class="visa-section__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2>Useful links</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="visa-links-intro">Most of these are sources for this page</div>

    <div class="visa-links-panel">
      {% for group in visaRules.usefulLinks %}
      <div class="visa-links-group">
        <div class="visa-links-group__title">{{ group.title }}</div>
        {% for link in group.links %}
        <div class="visa-link-block">
          {% if link.internal %}<a class="visa-link-block__internal" href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.label }} →</a>{% else %}<a href="{{ link.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ link.label }} ↗</a>{% endif %}
          <span class="visa-source">{% if link.nowrap %}{{ link.source | replace(link.nowrap, '<span class="visa-nowrap">' + link.nowrap + '</span>') | safe }}{% else %}{{ link.source }}{% endif %}{% if link.date %} · {{ link.date }}{% endif %}</span>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
